        <body>
            <div xml:id="d529">

                <pb facs="0649" n="581" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg581"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>Mr. John C. Wright to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 21.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1867-05-02"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi>
                            2, 1867.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>:* * * <hi rendition="#italic">*</hi> *</p>
                <p>The Prussian Ghanibers were opened on the 29th ultimo by his Majesty in person.
                    Enclosed will be found his speech in German and a translation of the same. The
                    Chambers are only called together to accept the constitution. They will likely
                    pass it <hi rendition="#italic">en bloc</hi> and adjourn for three weeks, as an
                    interval of twenty-one days is required before the second reading can take
                    place.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with great respect, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN C. WRIGHT.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d529-a1.xml" xpointer="d529-a1"/>
